# Authentik-specific, NON-SECRET config. This file IS committed.
#
# Shared values (TZ/CONFIG_ROOT/ADMIN_DOMAIN) live in ../../common.env.
# The two secrets are Komodo Variables — see komodo/resources/stacks.toml.
#
# ── FIRST DEPLOY: THE SETUP URL IS NOT THE HOMEPAGE ─────────────────────
#
# A fresh Authentik has no users at all, and the login page will not let you
# create one. Go to the initial-setup path instead, ONCE:
#
#   https://auth.admin.jjventer.co.za/if/flow/initial-setup/
#
# That creates the `akadmin` account and asks for its password. The URL stops
# working after the account exists.
#
# ⚠️ Set up a passkey immediately after: Settings > MFA Devices > WebAuthn.
# The passkey is the "unlock everything with the on-device key" behaviour, and
# it is worth registering while there is still only one account to fix if it
# goes wrong.
#
# ── Putting a service behind it ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Two mechanisms, and choosing the wrong one wastes an afternoon:
#
#   OIDC          The app redirects to Authentik, gets back a signed token,
#                 and knows WHO you are. Real per-user accounts. Use it
#                 wherever the app supports it: Immich, Seerr, Grafana.
#                 In Authentik: create an OAuth2/OpenID Provider.
#
#   Forward auth  Traefik asks Authentik "is this person logged in?" before
#                 passing the request on. The app learns nothing about who
#                 you are and keeps its own accounts. Use it only for apps
#                 with no OIDC support: the *arr stack, qbittorrent, tdarr.
#                 In Authentik: create a Proxy Provider in forward-auth mode.
#
# For forward auth, the order matters and step 2 is easy to get wrong:
#
#   1. Authentik UI: Proxy Provider (forward auth, single application), then
#      an Application bound to it, then add that Application to the
#      "authentik Embedded Outpost".
#   2. Uncomment the `authentik` middleware in
#      ../traefik/dynamic/middlewares.yml, then DEPLOY THE TRAEFIK STACK BY
#      HAND. Editing dynamic/*.yml does not redeploy traefik on its own, so
#      Traefik keeps reading its old clone and the middleware appears not to
#      exist. See ../traefik/dynamic/komodo.yml for why.
#   3. Add `middlewares=authentik@file` to the target service's router label,
#      and a second router on that host for PathPrefix(`/outpost.goauthentik.io/`)
#      pointing at authentik-server:9000, at a HIGHER priority than the app's
#      own router. Without that second router the auth callback hits the app
#      instead of Authentik and the login never completes.
#
# ⚠️ An unresolvable middleware breaks EVERY route through the websecure
# entrypoint, not just the one that names it. Never uncomment step 2 before
# this stack is actually running.
#
# ── The *arr apps need one more change ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Sonarr/Radarr/Prowlarr keep their own login on top of forward auth, so you
# would authenticate twice. Set, per app, in Settings > General > Security:
#
#   Authentication:          External / Forms
#   Authentication Required: Disabled for Local Addresses
#
# jjserver's Sonarr already runs with exactly that pair, so this is a
# carry-over rather than a new idea.

# Nothing else Authentik-specific needed yet.
